            {
              "id": "1771852607814",
              "name": "priceHoldEmailTemplate",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Dear <Customer Name>,\n\nWe have repriced PO <PO Number> against the current published prices. The price variance is less than <Price_Variance_Threshold> %, and per our pricing policy, we are able to proceed without requiring a revised PO.\n\nUpdated Order Details:\n\nLine Item  |\tCurrent Unit Price  |\tQuantity  |\tExtended Total\n<Item 1>   |\t <Order Price 1>\t   |    <Qty 1>\t  |        <Total 1>\n<Item 2>\t…\t…\t…\n\nNew Order Total:  <NewOrderTotal>\n\n\nThank you,\n<Logged in user>"
            },
            {
              "id": "1769751666388",
              "name": "priceHoldEmailTemplateFornewPO",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Dear <Customer Name>,\n\nOur system has repriced your purchase order <PO Number> using the current prices. One or more items show a price variance greater than or equal to <Price_Variance_Threshold> %, which exceeds the contractual tolerance threshold.\n\nSummary of Variance:\n\nLine Item   |\tPO Unit Price   |\tCurrent Price       |\tVariance %\n<Item 1>    |\t<PO Price 1>    |\t<Order Price 1>   |\t       <Variance 1>%\n<Item 2>\t…\t…\t…\n\nBecause the order total variance greater than or equal to <Price_Variance_Threshold> %, we have placed the order on Price Hold. To proceed, please create a new purchase order reflecting the current prices listed above and resubmit it to us.\n\nWe appreciate your prompt attention. Please let us know if you have questions or need assistance preparing the new PO.\n\nKind regards,\n<Logged In User>"
            },
