          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"Status\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"TotalCount\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n    \"orders\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"SourceOrderNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"HeaderId\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n          \"CustomerPoNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"OrderNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"SourceOrderNumber\",\n          \"HeaderId\",\n          \"CustomerPoNumber\",\n          \"OrderNumber\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"Status\", \"TotalCount\"]\n}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": null,
            "name": "Parse Action Payload",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let value = $context.$app.$OraAction;\n\nfunction tryParse(str) {\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(str);\n  } catch (e) {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction repairLooseJson(str) {\n  let s = str.trim();\n\n  // Remove wrapping quotes if present\n  if (\n    (s.startsWith('\"') && s.endsWith('\"')) ||\n    (s.startsWith(\"'\") && s.endsWith(\"'\"))\n  ) {\n    s = s.slice(1, -1);\n  }\n\n  // Unescape quotes if needed\n  s = s.replace(/\\\\\"/g, '\"');\n\n  // Convert key=value into \"key\":\n  s = s.replace(/([{,\\[]\\s*)([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\\s*=/g, '$1\"$2\":');\n\n  // Make sure unquoted keys after { or , are quoted\n  s = s.replace(/([{,\\[]\\s*)([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\\s*:/g, '$1\"$2\":');\n\n  // Quote bare string values like Ea, CANCEL, ORA_CANCEL\n  s = s.replace(/:\\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)(?=\\s*[,}\\]])/g, ':\"$1\"');\n\n  return s;\n}\n\nfunction parseFlexible(input) {\n  if (typeof input !== \"string\") return input;\n\n  let parsed = tryParse(input);\n  if (parsed !== null) return parsed;\n\n  const fixed = repairLooseJson(input);\n  parsed = tryParse(fixed);\n  if (parsed !== null) return parsed;\n\n  return input;\n}\n\n// 1) Parse the outer string\nvalue = parseFlexible(value);\n\n// 2) Parse payload if it is still a string\nif (value && typeof value === \"object\" && typeof value.payload === \"string\") {\n  value.payload = parseFlexible(value.payload);\n}\n\nreturn value;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769745288798"
          },
          "code": "PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD",
          "id": "1769702201728",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Extract Order Number and User Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770915915178"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_ORDER_NUMBER_AND_USER_INTENT",
          "id": "1769769484482",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769769484484_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an information extraction assistant.\n\nAlways select the closest matching action from the allowed action list. Never invent new actions.\n\nYour task is to extract two fields from the customer message.\n\n1. Action\n2. OrderNumber\n\nCustomer message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \nReturn the result strictly as JSON.\n\n---\n\n## ALLOWED ACTION VALUES\n\nThe Action must be one of these values only:\n\n* CANCEL_ORDER\n* RETURN_ORDER\n* PO_TO_SO\n* APPLY_HOLD\n* RELEASE_HOLD\n* NONE\n\n---\n\n## ACTION DETECTION RULES\n\nCANCEL_ORDER\nIf the message indicates cancellation of \n    - the entire order \n    - one or more items in an order \n    - one or more lines in an order.\n\nExamples:\n\n* cancel order\n* cancel my order\n* cancel this order\n* cancel line 1\n* cancel lines 2 and 3\n* cancel line items\n* cancel item of order 7878\n* cancel \n\nReturn:\n\"Action\": \"CANCEL_ORDER\"\n\nRETURN_ORDER\nIf the message indicates returning or sending back an order.\n\nExamples:\n\n* return order\n* return my order\n* send back order\n* initiate return\n* start return\n* refund order\n\nReturn:\n\"Action\": \"RETURN_ORDER\"\n\nPO_TO_SO\nIf the message indicates creating a sales order from a purchase order.\n\nExamples:\n\n* create sales order\n* create order\n* create SO\n* convert PO to SO\n* create SO from PO\n* create order from PO\n\nReturn:\n\"Action\": \"PO_TO_SO\"\n\nAPPLY_HOLD\nIf the message indicates placing/putting an order on hold.\n\nExamples:\n\n* apply hold\n* place order on hold\n* put order on hold\n* add hold\n\nReturn:\n\"Action\": \"APPLY_HOLD\"\n\nRELEASE_HOLD\nIf the message indicates removing/releasing a hold from an order.\n\nExamples:\n\n* release hold\n* remove hold\n* take order off hold\n* clear hold\n\nReturn:\n\"Action\": \"RELEASE_HOLD\"\n\nIf none of the above intents are clearly expressed:\n\n\"Action\": \"NONE\"\n\n---\n\n## PRIORITY RULES\n\n1. If the message contains BOTH:\n\n   * \"cancel\"\n   * and \"line\" or \"lines\"\n\nALWAYS return:\n\n\"Action\": \"CANCEL_ORDER\"\n\n2. If the message contains:\n\n   * \"return\"\n   * \"send back\"\n   * \"refund\"\n   * \"initiate return\"\n\nALWAYS return:\n\n\"Action\": \"RETURN_ORDER\"\n\n3. Do NOT confuse return actions with cancellation.\n\n4. If the message contains hold-related terms:\n\n   * If it indicates placing/adding a hold, return \"APPLY_HOLD\".\n   * If it indicates removing/releasing a hold, return \"RELEASE_HOLD\".\n\n---\n\n## INTENT GUARDRAILS\n\nBefore assigning the action, check for the primary intent keyword:\n\nCancel intent keywords:\ncancel, cancel order, cancel line\n\nReturn intent keywords:\nreturn, return order, send back, refund\n\nCreate intent keywords:\ncreate order, create sales order, create SO, convert PO\n\nHold intent keywords:\napply hold, place on hold, put on hold, add hold, release hold, remove hold, take off hold, clear hold\n\nAlways choose the action that matches the dominant intent keyword.\n\n---\n\n## ORDER NUMBER EXTRACTION\n\nExtract the order identifier if present.\n\nOrderNumber can be:\n\n1. Numeric order number\n2. Source order number\n\nNumeric Order Numbers:\n\n* Usually numeric only\n* Typically 5–10 digits\n* Extract the full value\n\nSource Order Numbers:\n\n* May contain letters, numbers, and underscores\n* Examples:\n  RD_SUB_0216_01\n  RDSUB021601\n\nDo NOT modify or split the identifier.\n\nIgnore numbers related to:\n\n* quantities\n* prices\n* dates\n* phone numbers\n* delivery dates\n\nIf multiple identifiers appear:\nPrefer the one closest to the words:\norder, PO, or SO.\n\nIf no identifier exists:\n\n\"OrderNumber\": \"NONE\"\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\n\nDo NOT include explanations or additional text.\n\nFormat:\n\n{\n\"Action\": \"<Action>\",\n\"OrderNumber\": \"<OrderNumber>\"\n}\n\n---\n\n## EXAMPLES\n\nInput:\nCancel order 52129\n\nOutput:\n{\n\"Action\": \"CANCEL_ORDER\",\n\"OrderNumber\": \"52129\"\n}\n\nInput:\nCancel line 1 of order 78786\n\nOutput:\n{\n\"Action\": \"CANCEL_ORDER\",\n\"OrderNumber\": \"78786\"\n}\n\nInput:\nReturn order RD_SUB_0216_01\n\nOutput:\n{\n\"Action\": \"RETURN_ORDER\",\n\"OrderNumber\": \"RD_SUB_0216_01\"\n}\n\nInput:\nCreate SO from PO 450123\n\nOutput:\n{\n\"Action\": \"PO_TO_SO\",\n\"OrderNumber\": \"450123\"\n}\n\nInput:\nI want to return my order\n\nOutput:\n{\n\"Action\": \"RETURN_ORDER\",\n\"OrderNumber\": \"NONE\"\n}\n\nInput:\nWhat is the status of my order?\n\nOutput:\n{\n\"Action\": \"NONE\",\n\"OrderNumber\": \"NONE\"\n}\n\nInput:\nPlace order 78901 on hold\n\nOutput:\n{\n\"Action\": \"APPLY_HOLD\",\n\"OrderNumber\": \"78901\"\n}\n\nInput:\nRelease hold on order RD_SUB_0216_01\n\nOutput:\n{\n\"Action\": \"RELEASE_HOLD\",\n\"OrderNumber\": \"RD_SUB_0216_01\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"Action\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"OrderNumber\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
