            },
            "name": "Render Priority Actions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "RENDER_PRIORITY_ACTIONS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772532413519",
          "id": "1769692421394",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769692421395_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an **Actionable Insight Generator** for Oracle Order Management data.\n\nYour task is to transform a service response containing sales orders into **actionable insight objects**.\n\n---\n\n### **Input**\n\nYou will receive a JSON payload -> {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_TOP_5_ORDERS_WITH_PRICE_HOLD.$output}} with the following structure:\n\n- A top-level `Status`\n- An `orders` array\n- Each order contains:\n  - `OrderNumber`\n  - `HeaderId`\n  - `SourceOrderNumber`\n\n---\n\n### **Processing Rules**\n\n1. If `Status` is not equal to \"SUCCESS\", do not render anything.\n2. If the `orders` array is empty or not present, do not render anything.\n3. Iterate over every element in `orders`.\n4. Generate exactly ONE actionable insight per order.\n5. Do NOT aggregate or merge multiple orders into a single insight.\n6. Do NOT invent or infer data not present in the input.\n\n---\n\n**Extract the \"Price Variance Threshold\" object present in {{$context.$nodes.READ_CUSTOMER_RAG_DATA_FOR_PRICE_VARIANCE.$output}} and assign it to: priceVarianceThreshold\n\nEXTRACTION RULES:\n1. The input may NOT be valid JSON (it may contain \"=\" instead of \":\" and unquoted keys).\n2. The input may contain multiple objects — ONLY extract data from the object that contains the \"Price Variance Threshold\" key.\n3. The \"Price Variance Threshold \" object will look like:\n   Price Variance Threshold ={...}\n4. Extract values EXACTLY as they appear:\n   - Do NOT modify text\n   - Do NOT trim or reformat\n   - Preserve symbols like % if present\n5. If multiple objects exist, select the one containing the \"Price Variance Threshold\" object.\n6. If a field is missing, return its value as null.\n7. Do NOT extract from \"chart\", \"customers\", or any other sections.\n8. Do NOT hallucinate values.\n9. priceVarianceThreshold has to be a number so remove any text or symbols like % or 'percentage' appended. Output Ex: priceVarianceThreshold: 0.2\n\n\n### **Output Requirements**\n\nGenerate priority actionable insight objects as below **if and only if `orders` array in the input is present and there are entries in it** else do not render any priority action.\n\nFor each entry in `orders` array when it is present in the input, generate an insight **must strictly following** the below schema:\n\n{\n  \"title\": \"Price Hold Applied on Order <OrderNumber>\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"This sales order has been placed on price hold pending your review.\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Review Price Hold Details\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Agent({\"action\":\"GetOrderDetails\",\"OrderNumber\":\"<OrderNumber>\",\"HeaderId\":\"<HeaderId>\",\"CustomerPoNumber\":\"<CustomerPoNumber>\",\"PriceVarianceThreshold\":\"<priceVarianceThreshold>\",\"ReleaseHoldComments\":\"<releaseHoldComments>\"})\",\n  \"priority\": true\n}\n\n---\n\n### **Field Rules to replace place holders with actual values in \"followUpCommand\"**\n\n- Replace `<OrderNumber>` with the value from `OrderNumber` in the input JSON.\n- Replace `<HeaderId>` with the value from `HeaderId` in the input JSON.\n- Replace `<CustomerPoNumber>` with the value from `CustomerPoNumber` in the input JSON.\n- Replace `<priceVarianceThreshold>` with the value of priceVarianceThreshold derived above from {{$context.$nodes.READ_CUSTOMER_RAG_DATA_FOR_PRICE_VARIANCE.$output}}\n- Replace `<releaseHoldComments >` with the value \"Hold released\".\n\n**VERY IMPORTANT AND NON-NEGOTIABLE: Do not miss replacing <OrderNumber>,<HeaderId>,<CustomerPoNumber>,<priceVarianceThreshold> and <releaseHoldComments> with their actual values in \"followUpCommand\" as mentioned above.\n---\n\n### **Output Constraints**\n\n- No markdown, comments, or explanations\n- No extra fields\n- Preserve array ordering from input\n- No actions to be generated if `orders` array is empty or does not present at all.\n\n---"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Render Nothing"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
