              "id": "1769746006309_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: {{$context.$nodes.RELEASE_HOLD.$output}}\n<ProcessId> -> Extract ProcessId from from Input\n-Generate a Card widget to mention that a release hold action has been performed.\n\n Subject: If <ProcessId> is available then \"Hold Release Request Submitted for Order {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.OrderNumber}}.\" else \"Hold Release Request Failed for Order {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.OrderNumber}}.\"\nSummary:  If <ProcessId> is available then redder \"Process ID <ProcessId> submitted. Please track the progress.\" else render \"{{$context.$nodes.RELEASE_HOLD.$output}}\" as it is.\nbadgeText: If <ProcessId> is available then \"Succcess\" else \"Error\"\nVariant: If <ProcessId> is available then \"info\" else \"error\"\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n**Never infer and assume any values for <ProcessId>. Always extract it from input.\n**Never render any other details other than Subject and Summary.\n**For all widgets and content, generate all the text including badges in InitCaps only"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Release Hold Error Details",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const errorJsonString = $context.$error.$errorMessage\nconst obj = JSON.parse(errorJsonString);\nconst status = obj.status;\nlet detail ;\nif(status == \"400\")\n{\n           detail = obj[\"o:errorDetails\"]?.[0]?.detail ?? null;\n}\nelse\n{\n          detail = \"Something went wrong while releasing hold. Please try again in a few moments.\" ;\n}\nreturn detail;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772083772602"
          },
