          "code": "CANCEL_ACTION_FAILURE_RESULT",
          "id": "1775961858455",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775961858464_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: {{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_CANCEL_WF_AS_PART_OF_CANCEL_AND_RETURN.$output.output}} \nMessage: {{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_CANCEL_WF_AS_PART_OF_CANCEL_AND_RETURN.$output.output}}\n\n-Generate a Card widget to mention that a Cancel Request has been performed.\n Subject: \"Cancel Request Failed for Order {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.OrderNumber}}.\"\nSummary: <Message>\nbadgeText:  \"Error\"\nVariant:  \"error\"\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n**Never infer and assume any values for <Message>. Always extract it from input.\n**Never render any other details other than Subject and Summary.\n**For all widgets and content, generate all the text including badges in InitCaps only"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Convert Return Payload to JSON object in Cancel and Return Flow",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "function isValidJSON(str) {\n  try {\n    JSON.parse(str);\n    return true;\n  } catch (e) {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction mapToJsonString(str) {\n  return str\n    .replace(/=/g, ':')\n    .replace(/([{,]\\s*)([A-Za-z0-9_]+):/g, '$1\"$2\":')\n    .replace(/:\\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)/g, ':\"$1\"');\n}\n\n// ===== MAIN LOGIC =====\n\nlet rawPayload = $context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.returnLinesPayload; \nlet finalPayload;\n\nif (typeof rawPayload === \"object\") {\n  //  already JSON object → stringify directly\n  finalPayload = JSON.stringify(rawPayload);\n\n} else if (typeof rawPayload === \"string\" && isValidJSON(rawPayload)) {\n  //  valid JSON string\n  finalPayload = rawPayload;\n\n} else if (typeof rawPayload === \"string\") {\n  //  map-style string → convert\n  const converted = mapToJsonString(rawPayload);\n  finalPayload = JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(converted));\n\n} else {\n  return rawPayload;\n}\n\nreturn finalPayload;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775961460231"
          },
          "code": "CONVERT_RETURN_PAYLOAD_TO_JSON_OBJECT_IN_CANCEL_AND_RETURN_FLOW",
          "id": "1776131618602",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "PO Data Check"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1771568862993",
            "false": "1770954494079"
          },
          "code": "PO_DATA_CHECK",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1771568746471",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771568746473_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.GET_PO_DATA_LENGTH.$output.result == 0}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1775367234187",
            "name": "Get Cancel Reason Description",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "// Read inputs from context\nconst items = $context.$nodes.GET_CANCEL_REASON_CODES.$output.LookupData;\nconst lookupCode = $context.$nodes.GET_DEFAULT_CANCEL_REASON_CODE.$output.defaultCancelReason;\n\nlet response = {\n  LookupCode: null,\n  Meaning: null,\n  Description: null\n};\n\nif (Array.isArray(items) && lookupCode != null) {\n  const item = items.find(\n    (x) => String(x.LookupCode).trim() === String(lookupCode).trim()\n  );\n\n  if (item) {\n    response = {\n      LookupCode: item.LookupCode ?? null,\n      Meaning: item.Meaning ?? null,\n      Description: item.Description ?? null\n    };\n  }\n}\n\nreturn  response;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775965265561"
          },
          "code": "GET_CANCEL_REASON_DESCRIPTION",
          "id": "1775146686772",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1773826578512",
            "name": "Get Return Reason And Type Meaning",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const returnReasons = $context.$nodes.GET_RETURN_REASON_CODES.$output.LookupData|| [];\nconst returnTypes = $context.$nodes.GET_RETURN_TYPES.$output.LookupData|| [];\n\nconst defaultReturnReasonCode =\n  $context.$nodes.GET_DEFAULT_RETURN_REASON_CODE_AND_TYPE.$output.defaultReturnReason;\n\nconst defaultReturnTypeCode =\n  $context.$nodes.GET_DEFAULT_RETURN_REASON_CODE_AND_TYPE.$output.defaultReturnMethod;\n\nconst returnReasonMappings =\n  $context.$nodes.GET_DEFAULT_RETURN_REASON_CODE_AND_TYPE.$output.returnReasonMappings || [];\n\n// Helper\nfunction getDetailsByLookupCode(items, code) {\n  if (!code) return { Meaning: null, Description: null };\n\n  const match = items.find(item => item?.LookupCode === code);\n\n  return match\n    ? {\n        Meaning: match.Meaning || null,\n        Description: match.Description || null\n      }\n    : {\n        Meaning: null,\n        Description: null\n      };\n}\n\n// Default values\nconst reasonDetails = getDetailsByLookupCode(returnReasons, defaultReturnReasonCode);\nconst typeDetails = getDetailsByLookupCode(returnTypes, defaultReturnTypeCode);\n\n// Enrich mappings\nconst enrichedReturnReasonMappings = Array.isArray(returnReasonMappings)\n  ? returnReasonMappings.map(mapping => {\n      const reason = getDetailsByLookupCode(returnReasons, mapping?.returnReasonCode);\n      const method = getDetailsByLookupCode(returnTypes, mapping?.returnMethodCode);\n\n      return {\n        returnReasonCode: mapping?.returnReasonCode || null,\n        returnReasonMeaning: reason.Meaning,\n        returnReasonDescription: reason.Description,\n\n        returnMethodCode: mapping?.returnMethodCode || null,\n        returnMethodMeaning: method.Meaning,\n        returnMethodDescription: method.Description\n      };\n    })\n  : null;\n\n// Final output\nconst output = {\n  defaultReturnReasonCode,\n  defaultReturnReasonMeaning: reasonDetails.Meaning,\n  defaultReturnReasonDescription: reasonDetails.Description,\n\n  defaultReturnTypeCode,\n  defaultReturnTypeMeaning: typeDetails.Meaning,\n  defaultReturnTypeDescription: typeDetails.Description,\n\n  returnReasonMappings: enrichedReturnReasonMappings\n};\n\nreturn output;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773731001523"
          },
          "code": "GET_RETURN_REASON_AND_TYPE_MEANING",
          "id": "1775707995749",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "DisplayReleaseHoldConfirmation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAYRELEASEHOLDCONFIRMATION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776603697069",
          "id": "1776498368389",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776498368390_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "CONTEXT BINDINGS\n- OrderNumber := {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_ORDER_NUMBER_AND_USER_INTENT.$output.OrderNumber}}\n- HeaderId := {{$context.$nodes.DERIVE_HEADER_ID.$output.result}}\n- ActionableHolds := {{$context.$nodes.FUZZY_MATCH_USER_HOLD.$output.items}}\n- NonActionableHolds := {{$context.$nodes.FUZZY_MATCH_USER_HOLD_FOR_NON_ACTIONABLE_HOLDS.$output.items}}\n- ActionableMatchFound := {{$context.$nodes.FUZZY_MATCH_USER_HOLD.$output.matchFound}}\n- NonActionableMatchFound := {{$context.$nodes.FUZZY_MATCH_USER_HOLD_FOR_NON_ACTIONABLE_HOLDS.$output.matchFound}}\n\n**HoldComment derivation instruction:**\n\nFrom {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}, extract a concise reason for releasing the hold.\n\nGuidelines:\n- Return ONLY the reason for releasing the hold (not the full sentence)\n- Remove order numbers, hold names, and command phrases like \"release hold\"\n- If the user provides a clear reason (e.g., \"because payment is received\"), return only that reason: \"payment is received\"\n- If the user provides a general statement (e.g., \"release the hold, customer confirmed\"), return the meaningful reason: \"customer confirmed\"\n- If no clear reason is present, return an empty string\n- Output must be plain text (no quotes, no JSON)\n\nReturn the extracted value and assign it to HoldComment.\nHoldComment must be available for substitution in the widget.\n\n\nRENDER RULES (Release Hold - Confirmation)\n\n1) Render one MessageListWidget for ActionableHolds.\n   For each actionableHold in ActionableHolds, generate a MessageListWidget entry with:\n   - Title: {{actionableHold.HoldName}}\n   - badgeText: \"Release Hold\"\n   - Timestamp: {{new Date(actionableHold.ApplyDate).toLocaleString('en-US',{month:'numeric',day:'numeric',year:'2-digit',hour:'numeric',minute:'numeric',hour12:true})}}\nReplace <ApplyDate> with the actionableHold item's ApplyDate value directly, without extra quotes or brackets, to ensure correct Date parsing. Format: M/D/YY H:MM AM/PM (e.g., 4/18/26 6:18 AM)\n   - Summary:\n     - Description: {{actionableHold.HoldDescription}}\n     - Comments: \"<HoldComment>\"\n     - Applied By: {{actionableHold.CreatedBy}}\n\n   Include an actionable insight within the same MessageListWidget entry with:\n   - Title: \"Release Order Hold\"\n   - shortDescription: \"Release Order Hold\"\n   - actionText: \"Release Hold\"\n   - followUpCommand: ora.Agent({\n       \"action\":\"RELEASE_HOLD\",\n       \"OrderNumber\":\"{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_ORDER_NUMBER_AND_USER_INTENT.$output.OrderNumber}}\",\n       \"HeaderId\":\"{{$context.$nodes.DERIVE_HEADER_ID.$output.result}}\",\n       \"HoldCode\":\"{{actionableHold.HoldCode}}\", \n       \"HoldComment\" : \"<HoldComment>\",\n     })\n  Note: Always replace <HoldComment> with the exact value of the HoldComment variable extracted from the user input message, ensuring proper escaping and formatting to prevent injection or parsing errors.\n\n2) Render one MessageListWidget for NonActionableHolds.\n   For each nonActionableHold in NonActionableHolds, generate a MessageListWidget entry with:\n   - Title: {{nonActionableHold.HoldName}}\n   - badgeText: \"Active Hold\"\n   - Timestamp: {{new Date(nonActionableHold.ApplyDate).toLocaleString('en-US',{month:'numeric',day:'numeric',year:'2-digit',hour:'numeric',minute:'numeric',hour12:true})}}\n   - Summary:\n     - Description: {{nonActionableHold.HoldDescription}}\n     - Comments: \"<HoldComment>\"\n     - Applied By: {{nonActionableHold.CreatedBy}}\n\n   Do not include any actionable insight or release button for NonActionableHolds.\n\n3) If ActionableMatchFound = false and NonActionableMatchFound = false,\n   show this message above the lists:\n   \"We could not find the requested holds, below are the current active holds.\"\n\nIMPORTANT RULES\n- Replace all placeholders with values from CONTEXT BINDINGS and the current hold item.\n- Do not use the generic variable name hold.\n- Use actionableHold only for ActionableHolds.\n- Use nonActionableHold only for NonActionableHolds.\n- If HoldComment is null, render an empty value.\n- Do not output anything outside widget definitions.\n- Do not combine the two lists into one loop.\n- Keep release actions only on ActionableHolds.\n- Rendering only."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CARD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "No Holds Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "NO_HOLDS_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1776603807946",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776603807955_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a Card widget to indicate that there are no holds found on the order with following details:\nSubject: No active holds found on the order"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CARD",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": true,
              "customNotes": "**Generate empty title.\n**Do not generate any content outside the card widget."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Summarize Order Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_ORDER_DETAILS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769746127455",
          "id": "1769702395199",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769702395200_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input:\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_PRICE_DETAILS.$output}}\n\nCustomer_Email = {{$context.$nodes.GET_CUSTOMER_EMAIL_ADDRESS.$output.result}}\n\n### GLOBAL EXECUTION CONTRACT (STRICT - NON NEGOTIABLE)\n\nYou MUST generate ALL of the following in final output:\n\n1. Widget 1 (Card Widget)\n2. Widget 2 (Multi Record Widget)\n3. Email Communication (<oraComms> block) - Generate this only when Customer_Email is present and not empty.\n\n- Skipping ANY of the above is INVALID output\n- Execution order MUST be:\n  1 → Widget 1\n  2 → Widget 2\n  3 → <oraComms>\n\n- Do NOT stop after Widget 1\n- Do NOT skip Widget 2\n- Do NOT skip Email generation when Customer_Email is present and not empty\n\n\n**Replace <ProductDescription>, <OrderedQuantity>, <OrderedUom>, <LineAmount> and <PurchaseOrderLineAmount> with values from Input.\n\n### CALCULATION (STRICT - VARIABLE BINDING)\n\nRead data ONLY from:\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_PRICE_DETAILS.$output}}\n\nFrom each object in \"lines\" array:\n\n- Read <LineAmount>\n- Read <PurchaseOrderLineAmount>\n\n### STEP 1: AGGREGATION\n\nTotalLineAmount = SUM of all <LineAmount> from lines array  \nTotalPurchaseOrderLineAmount = SUM of all <PurchaseOrderLineAmount> from lines array  \n\n### STEP 2: FINAL COMPUTATION\n\nTotalVariance = Absolute Value of  ((TotalPurchaseOrderLineAmount - TotalLineAmount) / TotalLineAmount) * 100\nTotalVariance can never be negative. It needs to be an absolute value.\n\n### STEP 3: VARIABLE BINDING (CRITICAL)\n\n- Treat TotalVariance as a FIXED VARIABLE\n- Store it as: VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE\n\n### STRICT RULES\n\n- VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE MUST be used everywhere\n- DO NOT recompute TotalVariance again\n- DO NOT derive from summary or other fields\n- DO NOT approximate or round\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nWidget 1:\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nGenerate a Card Widget with order-level information.\n\nSubject: Sales Order {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.OrderNumber}}\n\nSummary:\nThis order is on hold due to a price discrepancy between the Purchase Order and the Sales Order. Please review the details below. \nbadgeText: \"Price Hold\"\nVariant: \"warning\"\n\n\n### ACTIONABLE INSIGHT RULE (VARIABLE-DRIVEN - ABSOLUTE)\n\nUse ONLY the precomputed variable:\nVAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 1: TYPE ENFORCEMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Treat VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE as a NUMBER\n- Do NOT treat it as string\n- Do NOT round\n- Do NOT change precision\n- Do NOT convert units\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 2: BOOLEAN DERIVATION (SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCompute EXACTLY once:\n\nIS_BELOW_THRESHOLD = TRUE  if VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE < {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.PriceVarianceThreshold}}\nIS_BELOW_THRESHOLD = FALSE if VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE >= {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.PriceVarianceThreshold}}  \n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 3: HARD LOCK (CRITICAL)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- IS_BELOW_THRESHOLD is FINAL and IMMUTABLE\n- DO NOT recompute it\n- DO NOT re-evaluate VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE again\n- DO NOT override this decision later\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 4: STRICT OUTPUT GATING (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou are ONLY allowed to generate actionable insight IF IS_BELOW_THRESHOLD == TRUE\n\nIf IS_BELOW_THRESHOLD == FALSE:\n- Action generation is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 5: ACTION TEMPLATE (USE EXACTLY AS IS)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIF IS_BELOW_THRESHOLD == TRUE Then:\nGenerate actionable insight **inside the Card widget** with following details:\n{\n  \"title\": \"Release Price Hold\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Release Price Hold\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Agent({\\\"action\\\":\\\"ReleasePriceHold\\\",\\\"OrderNumber\\\":\\\"<OrderNumber>\\\",\\\"HeaderId\\\":\\\"<HeaderId>\\\",\\\"HoldCode\\\":\\\"<HoldCode>\\\"})\"\n}\n**IMPORTANT AND STRICT RULE: When **IS_BELOW_THRESHOLD = FALSE then do not generate any action or link** in Card Widget 1.\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 6: FORCED VALIDATION (SELF-CORRECTION)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore returning final output:\n\nCASE 1:\nIF VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE >= {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.PriceVarianceThreshold}} AND action exists:\n- REMOVE action completely\n- Ensure NO \"title\", \"actionText\", \"followUpCommand\" present\n\nCASE 2:\nIF VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE < {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.PriceVarianceThreshold}} AND action is missing:\n- ADD the action using exact template\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 7: EDGE CASE ENFORCEMENT (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE = 0.5 → IS_BELOW_THRESHOLD = FALSE\n- VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE > 0.5 → IS_BELOW_THRESHOLD = FALSE\n- ONLY values STRICTLY LESS than 0.5 are TRUE\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 8: BINDING EXAMPLES (DO NOT IGNORE)\n--------------------------------------------------\nExample:\nIF {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.PriceVarianceThreshold}} is 0.5 then\n- 0.007006666666666667 → TRUE → ACTION MUST EXIST ✅\n- 0.49 → TRUE → ACTION MUST EXIST ✅\n- 0.5 → FALSE → NO ACTION ❌\n- 0.50001 → FALSE → NO ACTION ❌\n**Do  not consider this example as actual values but for reference to decide whether to generate the action insight or not.\n--------------------------------------------------\nFINAL RULE (ABSOLUTE)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe presence of actionable insight MUST EXACTLY match:\n\n(VAR_TOTAL_VARIANCE < {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.PriceVarianceThreshold}} )\n\nIf mismatch detected → FIX before output.\n\n### FIELD SUBSTITUTION RULES (STRICT)\n\n- <OrderNumber> → {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.OrderNumber}}\n- <HeaderId> → {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.HeaderId}}\n- <HoldCode> → from input HoldCode field\n\n- DO NOT invent or infer values\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nWidget 2:\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n### WIDGET 2 RULE (MANDATORY)\n\n- You MUST ALWAYS generate Widget 2\n- This is NOT conditional\n- If no mismatched lines → return empty rows\n\nGenerate a Multi record widget with cols:\n\"Product\",\"Ordered Quantity\",\"UOM\",\"Sales Order Price\",\"Purchase Order Price\",\"Variance\"\n\nFor each object in lines array from input:\n- INCLUDE ONLY lines where isLineAmountMismatched = true\n\nMapping:\n- Product → <ProductDescription>\n- Ordered Quantity → <OrderedQuantity>\n- UOM → <OrderedUom>\n- Sales Order Price → <LineAmount>\n- Purchase Order Price → <PurchaseOrderLineAmount>\n- Variance → <Variance> %\n\n- Add Currency symbol for <LineAmount> and <PurchaseOrderLineAmount> values in above table.\n- **You must use currency symbol using <CurrencyCode> from lines object array from the input. Do not add the <CurrencyCode> as it is.\n-IMPORTANT AND NON-NEGOTIABLE: \n         - <ProductDescription>,<OrderedQuantity>, <OrderedUom>,<LineAmount>,<PurchaseOrderLineAmount> and <Variance> always have to be replaced only with the values from orders.lines array from input {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_PRICE_DETAILS.$output}} only.\n         - Never assume or later the values.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nEMAIL GENERATION (MANDATORY) only when Customer_Email is present and not empty\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n### EMAIL RULE (STRICT - NON NEGOTIABLE)\n\n- You MUST ALWAYS generate <oraComms>\n- Email is NOT optional when Customer_Email is present and not empty\n- It is independent of Widget 2\n\n### TEMPLATE SELECTION\n\nIF IS_BELOW_THRESHOLD = TRUE then\n→ Use {{$context.$variables.priceHoldEmailTemplate}}\n→ Also store \"Updated Pricing for PO # {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.CustomerPoNumber}}\" in EMAIL_SUBJECT as a VARIABLE\nELSE \n→ Use {{$context.$variables.priceHoldEmailTemplateFornewPO}}\n→ Also store \"Action Required – Price Variance Exceeds {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.PriceVarianceThreshold}} % for PO # {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.CustomerPoNumber}}\" in EMAIL_SUBJECT as a VARIABLE\n\n- EXACTLY ONE template must be used\n\n **TEMPLATE RULES: \n    - Use {{$context.$variables.priceHoldEmailTemplate}} when TotalVariance is less than threshold in which case IS_BELOW_THRESHOLD is TRUE\n\t- Use {{$context.$variables.priceHoldEmailTemplateFornewPO}} when TotalVariance is equal or greater than threshold in which case IS_BELOW_THRESHOLD is FALSE\n    - Do not miss these conditions and must be followed without any exceptions.\n\n### EMAIL CONTENT RULES\n\nReplace:\n - <Customer Name> with {{$context.$nodes.GET_CUSTOMER_NAME.$output.result}} \n- <PO Number> with {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.CustomerPoNumber}}\n- <Logged in user> with {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}} \n- <Price_Variance_Threshold> with {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.PriceVarianceThreshold}} \n\nRender Line Details header in bold:\n\nCASE 1: TotalVariance >= {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.PriceVarianceThreshold}} \n**The below details must be rendered in a tabular format.\nLine Item | PO Unit Price | Current Price | Variance %\n\nUnder the Line Details header, display following fields for each line:\nLine Item: <ProductDescription>\nPO Unit Price: Compute per unit prince and assign only the value using: <PurchaseOrderLineAmount> / <OrderedQuantity>\nCurrent Price: Compute per unit prince and assign only the value using: <LineAmount> / <OrderedQuantity>\nVariance $: <Variance> %\n\nCASE 2: TotalVariance < {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.PriceVarianceThreshold}} \nLine Item | Current Unit Price | Quantity | Extended Total\n**The below details must be rendered in a tabular format.\n\nUnder the Line Details header, display following fields for each line:\nLine Item: <ProductDescription>\nCurrent Price: Compute per unit prince and assign only the value using: <LineAmount> / <OrderedQuantity>\nQuantity: <OrderedQuantity>\nExtended Total: <LineAmount>\n\nAnd reaplce <NewOrderTotal> with sum of all <LineAmount> of all lines.\n\n\n### STRICT CONTENT RULES\n\n- Use simple HTML (<p>, <b>, <br/>)\n- No JSON inside content\n- No internal field names\n- No speculation\n\n\n### oraComms OUTPUT (MANDATORY)\n\n<oraComms>\n{\n  \"title\": \"Send Price Variance Email\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"<One line summary>\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Send Email\",\n  \"type\": \"email\",\n  \"content\": \"<Generated Content>\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"email\",\n      \"title\": \"email address\",\n      \"defaultValue\": {{$context.$nodes.GET_CUSTOMER_EMAIL_ADDRESS.$output.result}}\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"subject\",\n      \"title\":  <EMAIL_SUBJECT>,\n      \"defaultValue\": <EMAIL_SUBJECT>\n    }\n  ]\n}\n</oraComms>\n** In <oraComms> JSON, replace <EMAIL_SUBJECT> with it's actual value.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nFINAL VALIDATION (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore returning output, verify:\n\n- Widget 1 is present\n- Widget 2 is present\n- <oraComms> is present only when Customer_Email is present and not empty\n\nIf ANY is missing → regenerate output\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nIMPORTANT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Always render Widget 1 and Widget 2\n- Always generate Email (<oraComms>) nly when Customer_Email is present and not empty\n\n- Generate empty title\n- Do not generate content outside widgets and <oraComms>\n- Do NOT skip any section"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
