              "id": "1775961804101_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Context:\nCANCEL_PROCESS_ID: Extract ProcessId from {{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_CANCEL_WF_AS_PART_OF_CANCEL_AND_RETURN.$output.output}} \nRETURN_PROCESS_ID:  Extract ProcessId from {{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_RETURN_WF_AS_PART_OF_CANCEL_AND_RETURN.$output.output}} \n\n-Generate a messageListWidget for following details:\n Subject: If <CANCEL_PROCESS_ID> is available then \"Cancel Request Submitted for Order {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.OrderNumber}}.\" else \"Cancel Request Failed for Order {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.OrderNumber}}.\"\nSummary:  If <CANCEL_PROCESS_ID> is available then redder \"Process ID <CANCEL_PROCESS_ID> submitted. Please track the progress.\" else render \"{{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_CANCEL_WF_AS_PART_OF_CANCEL_AND_RETURN.$output.output}} \" as it is.\nbadgeText: If <CANCEL_PROCESS_ID> is available then \"Success\" else \"Error\"\nVariant: If <CANCEL_PROCESS_ID> is available then \"info\" else \"error\"\n\n Subject: If <RETURN_PROCESS_ID> is available then \"Return Request Submitted for Order {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.OrderNumber}}.\" else \"Return Request Failed for Order {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_ACTION_PAYLOAD.$output.result.OrderNumber}}.\"\nSummary:  If <RETURN_PROCESS_ID> is available then redder \"Process ID <RETURN_PROCESS_ID> submitted. Please track the progress.\" else render \"{{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_RETURN_WF_AS_PART_OF_CANCEL_AND_RETURN.$output.output}} \" as it is.\nbadgeText: If <RETURN_PROCESS_ID> is available then \"Success\" else \"Error\"\nVariant: If <RETURN_PROCESS_ID> is available then \"info\" else \"error\"\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n**Never infer and assume any values for <CANCEL_PROCESS_ID> and <RETURN_PROCESS_ID>. Always replace with acutal values from Context.\n**Never render any other details other than Subject and Summary.\n**For all widgets and content, generate all the text including badges in InitCaps only"
