              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given the non-actionable holds list and a user message.\n\nNon-actionable holds:\n{{$context.$nodes.GETNONACTIONABLEHOLDCODEFORORDER.$output.items}}\n\nUser message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nTask:\n1. Read the user message and extract the hold intent or hold-related phrase.\n2. Perform a fuzzy match against the Non-actionable holds list using:\n   - HoldCode\n   - HoldName\n   - HoldDescription\n3. Return every hold that matches the user intent with a confidence of 80% or more.\n\nMatching rules:\n- If one or more holds match at 80% or higher, return all such matches.\n- Do not return holds below 80% confidence.\n- If no holds match at 80% or higher, return all non-actionable holds.\n- Do not invent, infer, or modify hold data.\n- Return only these fields from each matched hold row:\n  - HoldCode\n  - HoldName\n  - HoldDescription\n  - HoldComments\n  - ApplyDate\n  - CreatedBy\n  - HoldInstanceId\n\nIMPORTANT\n- Extract and return the exact values for the above fields from the matched hold row.\n- Ensure that the output JSON includes these fields with their correct values.\n\nOutput must be valid JSON and follow this schema:\n{\n  \"matchedCount\": number,\n  \"matchFound\": boolean,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"HoldCode\": string | null,\n      \"HoldName\": string | null,\n      \"HoldDescription\": string | null,\n      \"HoldComments\": string | null,\n      \"ApplyDate\": string | null,\n      \"CreatedBy\": string | null,\n      \"HoldInstanceId\": string | null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nOutput rules:\n- If one or more matches are found at 80% or higher, items must contain all matching hold objects.\n- If no match is found at 80% or higher, items must contain all non-actionable holds.\n- matchedCount must equal the number of objects in items.\n- matchFound must be true when one or more matches are found at 80% or higher, otherwise false.\n- Return JSON only. No markdown. No explanations."
