              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "RENDER ONLY \n\nCONTEXT BINDINGS\n- OrderNumber := {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_ORDER_NUMBER_AND_USER_INTENT.$output.OrderNumber}}\n- HeaderId := {{$context.$nodes.DERIVE_SINGLE_HEADER_ID.$output.result}}\n- MatchingHoldCodes := {{$context.$nodes.MATCHCLOSESTHOLDS.$output.MatchingHoldCodes}} \n\nDERIVED (within this node)\n- holdCodes := map(MatchingHoldCodes, m => ({\n    HoldName: m.HoldName,\n    HoldCode: m.HoldCode,\n    Scope: \"Order Header\",                          \n    MatchPercentage: Math.round(m.MatchPercentage)\n  }))\n- holdCodesCount := length(holdCodes)\n\n**HoldComments derivation instruction:**\n\nFrom {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}, extract a concise reason for placing the order on hold.\n\nGuidelines:\n- Return ONLY the reason for placing the hold (not the full sentence)\n- Remove command phrases like \"place hold\", \"apply hold\", \"put on hold\"\n- Remove order numbers, hold names, and system-related terms\n- Prefer the part of the sentence that explains WHY (typically after commas, dashes, or words like \"because\", \"due to\", \"since\", \"as\", \"for\")\n- If the user provides a reason (e.g., \"apply hold because address is invalid\"), return: \"address is invalid\"\n- If the user gives a descriptive phrase (e.g., \"put on fraud hold, suspicious activity detected\"), return: \"suspicious activity detected\"\n- If multiple phrases exist, return the most relevant reason only\n- If no clear reason is present, return an empty string\n\nOutput rules:\n- Plain text only (no quotes, no JSON)\n- Single line only\n\nSet the result to: HoldComments\n\n\nRENDER RULES (Apply Hold - Selection Only)\n1) Generate Hold Type Matches widget ONLY when holdCodesCount > 0. \n   1.1) Generate a multiRecordWidget with columns:\n       Title: 'Hold Type Matches'\n        Summary: ''\n        description: 'List of hold code candidates for order <OrderNumber>'\n        subtitle: 'Select to apply'\n\n       Row Mapping (for each candidate in holdCodes):\n         - Hold Name: <candidate.HoldName>\n         - Hold Code: <candidate.HoldCode>\n         - Details: \"Applies to: Order Header\"\n         - Match %: <candidate.MatchPercentage>%       \n         - Row action button label: 'Select' \n         - Action: 'Select' with followUpCommand:\n             ora.Agent({\n               \"action\":\"SELECT_HOLD_CANDIDATE\",\n               \"OrderNumber\":\"<OrderNumber>\",\n               \"HeaderId\":\"<HeaderId>\",\n               \"HoldCode\":\"<candidate.HoldCode>\",\n               \"HoldName\":\"<candidate.HoldName>\",\n               \"HoldDescription\":\"<candidate.HoldDescription>\",\n               \"MatchPercentage\":\"<candidate.MatchPercentage>\",\n               \"HoldComments\":\"<HoldComments>\",\n             })\n\n\n\nIMPORTANT RULES\n- Do not generate a messageListWidget.\n- Generate exactly one widget only.\n- Replace all placeholders with values from CONTEXT BINDINGS/DERIVED.\n- If HoldComments is null, pass empty string.\n- Do NOT generate any widget when holdCodesCount = 0.\n- If a HoldCode contains underscores, output it with zero-width spaces around each underscore to prevent italic rendering, while keeping the visible text unchanged.\n- Do NOT output anything outside widget definitions.\n- Rendering only."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
